,null,{}],\\\"templateStyles\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"templateScripts\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"notFound\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"forbidden\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"unauthorized\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\"}]]}],{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$1\\\",\\\"c\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$L4\\\",[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"script\\\",\\\"script-0\\\",{\\\"src\\\":\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\\\",\\\"async\\\":true,\\\"nonce\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\"}]],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L5\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$6\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Next.MetadataOutlet\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$@7\\\"}]}]]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,\\\"$@8\\\"]},null,false,\\\"$@8\\\"]},null,false,\\\"$@8\\\"]},null,false,null],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$1\\\",\\\"h\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[null,[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L9\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"$La\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"hidden\\\":true,\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lb\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$6\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Next.Metadata\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$Lc\\\"}]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"meta\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"next-size-adjust\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"\\\"}]]}],false]],\\\"m\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"G\\\":[\\\"$d\\\",[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"link\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"rel\\\":\\\"stylesheet\\\",\\\"href\\\":\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\\\",\\\"precedence\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"crossOrigin\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"nonce\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\"}]]],\\\"S\\\":true,\\\"h\\\":null,\\\"s\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"l\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"p\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"b\\\":\\\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\\\"}\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"e:[]\\n8:\\\"$We\\\"\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"f:I[22016,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\\\"],\\\"\\\"]\\n10:I[16505,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\\\"],\\\"LessonClient\\\"]\\n11:Tad8,\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"# Script Structure and Best Practices\\n\\nMoving from one-liners to full scripts requires understanding how PowerShell scripts are organized and what conventions make them maintainable.\\n\\n## Script Files and Execution Policy\\n\\nPowerShell scripts are saved as `.ps1` files. Before running scripts, you need an appropriate execution policy:\\n\\n```powershell\\nGet-ExecutionPolicy\\nSet-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser\\n```\\n\\n\\u003e **Key Concept:** `RemoteSigned` is the recommended policy for most users. It allows local scripts to run freely while requiring downloaded scripts to be signed.\\n\\n## The #Requires Statement\\n\\nPlace `#Requires` at the top of your script to enforce prerequisites. The script will not run if the requirements are not met:\\n\\n```powershell\\n#Requires -Version 7.0\\n#Requires -Modules ActiveDirectory\\n#Requires -RunAsAdministrator\\n```\\n\\n## Comment-Based Help\\n\\nAdd structured help so users can run `Get-Help` on your script. Place the comment block at the top of the file, before the `param` block:\\n\\n```powershell\\n\\u003c#\\n.SYNOPSIS\\n    Exports user data to a CSV file.\\n\\n.DESCRIPTION\\n    Retrieves user accounts from Active Directory and exports\\n    selected properties to a CSV file.\\n\\n.PARAMETER OutputPath\\n    The file path for the exported CSV.\\n\\n.EXAMPLE\\n    .\\\\Export-Users.ps1 -OutputPath C:\\\\Reports\\\\users.csv\\n#\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n## Script-Level Param Block\\n\\nDefine parameters at the top of the script using `param()`. This is how users pass arguments to your script:\\n\\n```powershell\\nparam(\\n    [Parameter(Mandatory)]\\n    [string]$OutputPath,\\n\\n    [int]$MaxResults = 100,\\n\\n    [switch]$IncludeDisabled\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## Regions and Organization\\n\\nUse `#region` and `#endregion` to create collapsible sections in your editor:\\n\\n```powershell\\n#region Configuration\\n$LogPath = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'logs'\\n$Date = Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd'\\n#endregion\\n\\n#region Main Logic\\n# Your core script logic here\\n#endregion\\n```\\n\\n\\u003e **Key Concept:** `$PSScriptRoot` is an automatic variable that contains the directory of the currently running script. Use it to build paths relative to the script location.\\n\\n## Naming Conventions\\n\\nFollow these community-standard conventions for readable scripts:\\n\\n- **Cmdlets and functions:** Use `Verb-Noun` format with approved verbs (`Get-Verb` lists them)\\n- **Variables:** Use `PascalCase` (e.g., `$UserName`, `$OutputPath`)\\n- **Parameters:** Use `PascalCase` with descriptive names\\n- **Script files:** Use `Verb-Noun.ps1` naming (e.g., `Export-UserReport.ps1`)\\n\\n## Putting It All Together\\n\\nA well-structured script follows this order:\\n\\n```powershell\\n#Requires -Version 7.0\\n\\n\\u003c#\\n.SYNOPSIS\\n    Brief description of the script.\\n#\\u003e\\n\\nparam(\\n    [Parameter(Mandatory)]\\n    [string]$InputPath\\n)\\n\\n#region Main Logic\\n# Script body here\\n#endregion\\n```\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"header\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lf\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/module/intermediate\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-4 w-4\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\",null,{\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\\\"}]}],\\\"Intermediate PowerShell\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lf\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/module/intermediate/rest-apis\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Working with REST APIs\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-4 w-4\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\",null,{\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\\\"}]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\\\",\\\"children\\\":[4,\\\" / \\\",6]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lf\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/module/intermediate/pssessions-and-remoting\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"PSSessions and Remoting\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-4 w-4\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\",null,{\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\\\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h1\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Script Structure and Best Practices\\\"}]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L10\\\",null,{\\\"lesson\\\":{\\\"meta\\\":{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Script Structure and Best Practices\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Organizing scripts for maintainability.\\\",\\\"slug\\\":\\\"script-structure\\\",\\\"order\\\":4,\\\"prerequisites\\\":[\\\"m2-l3\\\"]},\\\"content\\\":\\\"$11\\\",\\\"exercises\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"m2-l4-ex1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"syntax-check\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Write a #Requires statement that enforces PowerShell version 7.0 and requires the script to be run as administrator.\\\",\\\"hints\\\":[\\\"#Requires uses -Version to specify the minimum version.\\\",\\\"Use -RunAsAdministrator to require elevation.\\\",\\\"Each requirement can be on its own #Requires line.\\\"],\\\"validation\\\":[{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"#Requires\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Use the #Requires statement.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"-Version\\\\\\\\s+7\\\\\\\\.0\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Specify -Version 7.0.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"-RunAsAdministrator\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Add -RunAsAdministrator to require elevation.\\\"}],\\\"solution\\\":\\\"#Requires -Version 7.0\\\\n#Requires -RunAsAdministrator\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The #Requires statement prevents the script from running unless the conditions are met. -Version 7.0 ensures PowerShell 7+ and -RunAsAdministrator requires an elevated session.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"m2-l4-ex2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"syntax-check\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Write a comment-based help block with a .SYNOPSIS of 'Gets disk space report.' and a .PARAMETER section for a parameter called ComputerName described as 'The target computer.'\\\",\\\"hints\\\":[\\\"Comment-based help goes inside \\u003c# ... #\\u003e delimiters.\\\",\\\"Each keyword starts with a dot: .SYNOPSIS, .PARAMETER\\\",\\\"The parameter name goes on the same line as .PARAMETER.\\\"],\\\"validation\\\":[{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"\\u003c#\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Start the help block with \\u003c#.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\".SYNOPSIS\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Include the .SYNOPSIS keyword.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"Gets disk space report\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Set the synopsis to 'Gets disk space report.'\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\\.PARAMETER\\\\\\\\s+ComputerName\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Add .PARAMETER ComputerName on the same line.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"The target computer\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Describe the parameter as 'The target computer.'\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"#\\u003e\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Close the help block with #\\u003e.\\\"}],\\\"solution\\\":\\\"\\u003c#\\\\n.SYNOPSIS\\\\n    Gets disk space report.\\\\n\\\\n.PARAMETER ComputerName\\\\n    The target computer.\\\\n#\\u003e\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Comment-based help uses special keywords preceded by a dot. Get-Help reads these blocks and displays them in the standard help format. The .PARAMETER keyword name must match an actual parameter.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"m2-l4-ex3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"syntax-check\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Write a param() block with a mandatory string parameter called OutputPath and an optional integer parameter called MaxResults with a default value of 50.\\\",\\\"hints\\\":[\\\"Use [Parameter(Mandatory)] to make a parameter required.\\\",\\\"Type constraints go in square brackets: [string], [int].\\\",\\\"Default values are assigned with = after the parameter name.\\\"],\\\"validation\\\":[{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"param(\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Start with the param() keyword.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"[Parameter(Mandatory)]\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Use [Parameter(Mandatory)] to make the parameter required.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"[string]\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Declare OutputPath as [string] type.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"$$OutputPath\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Name the parameter $OutputPath.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"[int]\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Declare MaxResults as [int] type.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\\$MaxResults\\\\\\\\s*=\\\\\\\\s*50\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Set the default value of $MaxResults to 50.\\\"}],\\\"solution\\\":\\\"param(\\\\n    [Parameter(Mandatory)]\\\\n    [string]$OutputPath,\\\\n\\\\n    [int]$MaxResults = 50\\\\n)\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The param() block defines script or function parameters. [Parameter(Mandatory)] makes OutputPath required. $MaxResults defaults to 50 if not provided by the caller.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"m2-l4-ex4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"syntax-check\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Write the command to set the execution policy to RemoteSigned for the current user.\\\",\\\"hints\\\":[\\\"Use Set-ExecutionPolicy with -ExecutionPolicy.\\\",\\\"The scope should be CurrentUser.\\\",\\\"RemoteSigned allows local scripts but requires downloaded scripts to be signed.\\\"],\\\"validation\\\":[{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Set-ExecutionPolicy\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Use the Set-ExecutionPolicy cmdlet.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"contains\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"RemoteSigned\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Set the policy to RemoteSigned.\\\"},{\\\"rule\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"-Scope\\\\\\\\s+CurrentUser\\\",\\\"hintOnFail\\\":\\\"Use -Scope CurrentUser to apply it only to your user account.\\\"}],\\\"solution\\\":\\\"Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Set-ExecutionPolicy controls which scripts are allowed to run. RemoteSigned is the recommended policy for most users. -Scope CurrentUser avoids needing administrator privileges.\\\"}],\\\"moduleSlug\\\":\\\"intermediate\\\"}}],\\\"$L12\\\"]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"12:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"footer\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lf\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/module/intermediate/rest-apis\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\",null,{\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\\\"}]}],\\\"Working with REST APIs\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$Lf\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/module/intermediate/pssessions-and-remoting\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"PSSessions and Remoting\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\",null,{\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"d\\\":\\\"M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5M21 12H3\\\"}]}]]}]]}]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"a:[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"meta\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"charSet\\\":\\\"utf-8\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"meta\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"name\\\":\\\"viewport\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\"}]]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"13:I[27201,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\\\",\\\"/_