e described as 'The target computer.'\",\"hints\":[\"Comment-based help goes inside <# ... #> delimiters.\",\"Each keyword starts with a dot: .SYNOPSIS, .PARAMETER\",\"The parameter name goes on the same line as .PARAMETER.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"<#\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start the help block with <#.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\".SYNOPSIS\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Include the .SYNOPSIS keyword.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"Gets disk space report\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set the synopsis to 'Gets disk space report.'\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\.PARAMETER\\\\s+ComputerName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add .PARAMETER ComputerName on the same line.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"The target computer\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Describe the parameter as 'The target computer.'\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"#>\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Close the help block with #>.\"}],\"solution\":\"<#\\n.SYNOPSIS\\n    Gets disk space report.\\n\\n.PARAMETER ComputerName\\n    The target computer.\\n#>\",\"explanation\":\"Comment-based help uses special keywords preceded by a dot. Get-Help reads these blocks and displays them in the standard help format. The .PARAMETER keyword name must match an actual parameter.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l4-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a param() block with a mandatory string parameter called OutputPath and an optional integer parameter called MaxResults with a default value of 50.\",\"hints\":[\"Use [Parameter(Mandatory)] to make a parameter required.\",\"Type constraints go in square brackets: [string], [int].\",\"Default values are assigned with = after the parameter name.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"param(\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with the param() keyword.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"[Parameter(Mandatory)]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use [Parameter(Mandatory)] to make the parameter required.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"[string]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Declare OutputPath as [string] type.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"$$OutputPath\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Name the parameter $OutputPath.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"[int]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Declare MaxResults as [int] type.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$MaxResults\\\\s*=\\\\s*50\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set the default value of $MaxResults to 50.\"}],\"solution\":\"param(\\n    [Parameter(Mandatory)]\\n    [string]$OutputPath,\\n\\n    [int]$MaxResults = 50\\n)\",\"explanation\":\"The param() block defines script or function parameters. [Parameter(Mandatory)] makes OutputPath required. $MaxResults defaults to 50 if not provided by the caller.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l4-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command to set the execution policy to RemoteSigned for the current user.\",\"hints\":[\"Use Set-ExecutionPolicy with -ExecutionPolicy.\",\"The scope should be CurrentUser.\",\"RemoteSigned allows local scripts but requires downloaded scripts to be signed.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Set-ExecutionPolicy\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the Set-ExecutionPolicy cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"RemoteSigned\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set the policy to RemoteSigned.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-Scope\\\\s+CurrentUser\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -Scope CurrentUser to apply it only to your user account.\"}],\"solution\":\"Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser\",\"explanation\":\"Set-ExecutionPolicy controls which scripts are allowed to run. RemoteSigned is the recommended policy for most users. -Scope CurrentUser avoids needing administrator privileges.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"intermediate\"}}],\"$L5\"]}],[\"$L6\"],\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\n5:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children